{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And Abraham said to Sarah.</b> Here he did not instruct her to precede him and say 'my brother,' as he did when he went down to Egypt — for that is a place of the uncircumcised, and she would be extraordinary among them in her beauty, which is not so in Gerar. And therefore you will find that Avimelekh said to him, ״מָה רָאִיתָ כִּי עָשִׂיתָ אֶת הַדָּבָר הַזֶּה״ — something Pharaoh did not ask him, because Avimelekh's domain was not populated by the uncircumcised, and they possess beauty among themselves, and Sarah would not stand out so remarkably in her beauty; and therefore you will find that he agreed to dwell in his domain, which was not so with Pharaoh."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:23.981580566Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}